title: Microsoft Hyper-V Cluster: VM state
agents: windows
catalog: os/services
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the power state of the virtual machines of a Microsoft
 Windows failover cluster running Hyper-V and shows the node they run on.

 By default the check is {OK} if the VM is online and {WARN} if it is offline.
 The expected power state can be configured with the rule "Hyper-V cluster VM state".
 A failed VM is always {CRIT}, any other state is {UNKNOWN}.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_cluster.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V".

item:
 The name of the virtual machine.

discovery:
 One service is created for each clustered virtual machine.

cluster:
 Every cluster node reports all clustered virtual machines. In a Checkmk
 cluster host the most favourable report is shown.
